                     s_cov:100.0%, Eval:1.0e-280]"
                     /note="Domain:cl11971:PPK2 Polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2).
                     Members of this protein family belong to the polyphosphate
                     kinase 2 (PPK2) family, which is not related in sequence to
                     PPK1. While PPK1 tends to act in the biosynthesis of
                     polyphosphate, or poly(P), members of the PPK2 family tend
                     to use the terminal phosphate of poly(P) to regenerate ATP
                     or GTP from the corresponding nucleoside diphosphate, or
                     ADP from AMP as is the case with polyphosphate:AMP
                     phosphotransferase (PAP). Members of this protein family
                     most likely transfer the terminal phosphate between poly(P)
                     and some nucleotide, but it is not clear which. [Central
                     intermediary metabolism, Phosphorus compounds]
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:271-489, Eval:7.3e-102, score:303.9]"
                     /note="Domain:cl11971:PPK2 Polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2).
                     Members of this protein family belong to the polyphosphate
                     kinase 2 (PPK2) family, which is not related in sequence to
                     PPK1. While PPK1 tends to act in the biosynthesis of
                     polyphosphate, or poly(P), members of the PPK2 family tend
                     to use the terminal phosphate of poly(P) to regenerate ATP
                     or GTP from the corresponding nucleoside diphosphate, or
                     ADP from AMP as is the case with polyphosphate:AMP
                     phosphotransferase (PAP). Members of this protein family
                     most likely transfer the terminal phosphate between poly(P)
                     and some nucleotide, but it is not clear which. [Central
                     intermediary metabolism, Phosphorus compounds]
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:11-237, Eval:2.6e-47, score:162.5]"
                     /note="MGA_232"
