                     /note="Domain:cl26271:Phosphonate-bd ABC transporter,
                     phosphonate, periplasmic substrate-binding protein. Members
                     of this family ABC transporter periplasmic binding proteins
                     and represent one clade within a larger family that
                     includes phosphate, phosphite, and phosphonate
                     transporters. All members of the seed alignment occur near
                     a gene for SelD, the selenium-activating protein needed to
                     make selenocysteine or selenouridine. Context therefore
                     suggests members should be able to transport selenate,
                     although transporting other substrates as well (e.g.
                     phosphonates) is possible. This model has no overlap with
                     TIGR03431, whose members are found regularly with
                     phosphonate catabolism operons. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:9-278, Eval:2.8e-19, score:82.8]"
