                     /note="COG:COG1802:GntR DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator, GntR family [Category:K, Aligned:104-312,
                     Eval:1.0e-23, score:94.4]"
                     /note="Domain:cl28325:MngR DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator, GntR family [Transcription]. This family
                     consists of repressors of the GntR family typically
                     associated with trehalose utilization operons. Trehalose is
                     imported as trehalose-6-phosphate and then hydrolyzed by
                     alpha,alpha-phosphotrehalase to glucose and glucose-6-P.
                     This family includes repressors mostly from Gram-positive
                     lineages and does not include the TreR from E. coli.
                     [Regulatory functions, DNA interactions] [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:10-86, Eval:2.5e-08, score:50.7, C-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_427"
