                     /note="WP_005768135.1 OPT family oligopeptide transporter
                     (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:89.8%, q_cov:100.0%,
                     s_cov:100.0%, Eval:5.4e-300]"
                     /note="Domain:cl14607:OPT OPT oligopeptide transporter
                     protein. This protein represents a small family of integral
                     membrane proteins from Gram-negative bacteria, a
                     Gram-positive bacteria, and an archaeal species. Members of
                     this family contain 15 to 18 GES predicted transmembrane
                     regions, and this family has extensive homology to a family
                     of yeast tetrapeptide transporters, including isp4
                     (Schizosaccharomyces pombe) and Opt1 (Candida albicans).
                     EspB, an apparent equivalog from Myxococcus xanthus, shares
                     an operon with a two component system regulatory protein,
                     and is required for the normal timing of sporulation after
                     the aggregation of cells. This is consistent with a role in
                     transporting oligopeptides as signals across the membrane.
                     [Transport and binding proteins, Amino acids, peptides and
                     amines] [Superfamily, Aligned:14-567, Eval:1.5e-31,
                     score:126.3]"
                     /note="MGA_1480"
