                     /note="WP_011105543.1 CobW family GTP-binding protein
                     (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:81.7%, q_cov:99.7%,
                     s_cov:99.7%, Eval:1.2e-156]"
                     /note="Domain:cl26870:CobW_C Cobalamin synthesis protein
                     cobW C-terminal domain. The family of proteins identified
                     by this model is generally found proximal to the trimeric
                     cobaltochelatase subunit CobN which is essential for
                     vitamin B12 (cobalamin) biosynthesis. The protein contains
                     an P-loop nucleotide-binding loop in the N-terminal domain
                     and a histidine-rich region in the C-terminal portion
                     suggesting a role in metal binding, possibly as an
                     intermediary between the cobalt transport and chelation
                     systems. A broader CobW family is delineated by two Pfam
                     models which identify the N- and C-terminal domains
                     (pfam02492 and pfam07683). [Biosynthesis of cofactors,
                     prosthetic groups, and carriers, Heme, porphyrin, and
                     cobalamin] [Superfamily, Aligned:5-286, Eval:2.6e-47,
                     score:159.4]"
                     /note="MGA_1599"
