                     /note="Domain:cl01101:DsrC DsrC like protein. Members of
                     this protein family may be described as TusE, a partner to
                     TusBCD in a sulfur relay system for 2-thiouridine
                     biosynthesis, a tRNA base modification process. Other
                     members are DsrC, a functionally similar protein in species
                     where the sulfur relay system exists primarily for sulfur
                     metabolism rather than tRNA base modification. Some members
                     of this family are known explicitly as the gamma subunit of
                     sulfite reductases. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-111,
                     Eval:5.9e-50, score:151.4]"
