                     s_cov:96.5%, Eval:2.6e-141]"
                     /note="Domain:cl27046:CopB Copper resistance protein B
                     precursor (CopB). This family consists of several bacterial
                     copper resistance proteins. Copper is essential and serves
                     as cofactor for more than 30 enzymes yet a surplus of
                     copper is toxic and leads to radical formation and
                     oxidation of biomolecules. Therefore, copper homeostasis is
                     a key requisite for every organism. CopB serves to extrude
                     copper when it approaches toxic levels. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:26-287, Eval:1.5e-103, score:302.2, N-term
                     missing]"
                     /note="MGA_2407"
