                     /note="Domain:cl01907:YscJ_FliF Secretory protein of
                     YscJ/FliF family. All members of this protein family are
                     predicted lipoproteins with a conserved Cys near the
                     N-terminus for cleavage and modification, and are part of
                     known or predicted type III secretion systems. Members are
                     found in both plant and animal pathogens, including the
                     obligately intracellular chlamydial species and
                     (non-pathogenic) root nodule bacteria. The most closely
                     related proteins outside this family are examples of the
                     flagellar M-ring protein FliF. [Protein fate, Protein and
                     peptide secretion and trafficking, Cellular processes,
