                     /note="Domain:cl27048:BTP Chlorhexidine efflux transporter.
                     This family represents a conserved pair of two
                     transmembrane alpha-helices. All members carry the two
                     pairs of TMs. BTP is a form of drug efflux pump, that
                     actively tranports chlorhexidine out of the cell.
                     Chlorhexidine, a bisbiguanide antimicrobial agent, is
                     commonly used as an antiseptic and disinfectant in
                     hospitals, and there is an increasing problem with
                     resistance to it in some pathogenic bacteria. BTP is
                     localized in the cytoplasmic membrane. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:13-156, Eval:9.5e-54, score:164.5]"
                     /note="MGA_3143"
