                     formation in bacterial cell division. Its C-terminal domain
                     binds FtsZ, a major component of the bacterial septal ring.
                     The structure of this domain is an alpha-beta fold with
                     three alpha helices and a beta sheet of six antiparallel
                     beta strands. The major loops protruding from the beta
                     sheet surface are thought to form a binding site for FtsZ.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:3-281, Eval:3.2e-78, score:237.8]"
