                     2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-ureidoimidazoline decarboxylase
                     (Pseudomonas syringae group genomosp. 3) [pid:88.1%,
                     q_cov:100.0%, s_cov:100.0%, Eval:3.7e-86]"
                     /note="Domain:cl01251:OHCU_decarbox OHCU decarboxylase.
                     Previously thought to only proceed spontaneously, the
                     decarboxylation of
                     2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy--5-ureidoimidazoline (OHCU) has
                     been recently been shown to be catalyzed by this enzyme in
                     Mus musculus. Homologs of this enzyme are found adjacent to
                     and fused with uricase in a number of prokaryotes and are
                     represented by this model. This model is a separate (but
                     related) clade from that represented by TIGR3164. This
                     model places a second homolog in streptomyces species which
                     (are not in the vicinity of other urate catabolism
                     associated genes) below the trusted cutoff. [Superfamily,
                     Aligned:1-171, Eval:3.0e-73, score:215.3]"
                     /note="MGA_3208"
